# Normalize every text file to LF in the repository AND check it out as LF on
# every platform, Windows included.
#
# Why this is not optional: Git's Windows default (`core.autocrlf=true`)
# rewrites text files to CRLF on checkout. Anything COPYed from that working
# tree into a Linux container image then carries CRLF, and a shell script whose
# shebang reads `#!/bin/sh\r` fails to exec with a bare
# "No such file or directory" — the interpreter path itself is wrong.
#
# That is exactly how `docker/worker/entrypoint.sh` silently stopped booting the
# ACA worker on 2026-07-27: the sandbox reported `Running` (ACA's own
# `tini -- sleep infinity` keep-alive is PID 1 regardless), no worker process
# ever started, nothing dialed the router, and the Linear delegation hung with
# no error logged anywhere. The committed blob was correct LF the whole time —
# only the Windows checkout was corrupt, so CI-built images worked and
# locally-built ones did not.
#
# Guarded by packages/router/test/worker-entrypoint-line-endings.test.ts.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt-and-braces for the executable assets that actually get COPYed into an
# image and run. Listed explicitly so the protection survives any future
# narrowing of the blanket rule above.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.cjs text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile text eol=lf

# Binary types: never apply EOL conversion. The repo tracks no binaries today;
# these are here so adding one later cannot corrupt it.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.tgz binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.node binary
*.wasm binary
